cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "markov-chain-monte-carlo: A composable MCMC framework for Rust"
version: "0.3.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20033111
url: "https://github.com/acgetchell/markov-chain-monte-carlo"
repository-code: "https://github.com/acgetchell/markov-chain-monte-carlo"
authors:
  - family-names: "Getchell"
    given-names: "Adam"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0797-0021"
keywords:
  - "markov-chain-monte-carlo"
  - "mcmc"
  - "metropolis-hastings"
  - "monte-carlo"
  - "sampling"
abstract: >-
  markov-chain-monte-carlo is a Rust library providing composable
  Metropolis-Hastings sampling over arbitrary state spaces, with by-value,
  in-place, and delayed-commit proposal APIs, log-space transition handling,
  observable measurement utilities, streaming statistics, checkpointing, and
  proposal-validation diagnostics.
